---
/**
 * Credentials page, diagram 2: which value wins when a token is set in more
 * than one place. Mirrors Configuration Precedence in CLAUDE.md.
 */
import '../styles/diagrams.css';
---

<figure class="not-prose my-8">
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 210" role="img" aria-labelledby="cp-title cp-desc" class="dg w-full min-w-[600px] h-auto">
      <title id="cp-title">Which token wins</title>
      <desc id="cp-desc">
        pncli takes the first value it finds: a PNCLI_ environment variable, then a well-known CI variable such as
        GITHUB_TOKEN, SONAR_TOKEN or SYSTEM_ACCESSTOKEN, then the global config file, where the value is either
        plaintext or a keychain reference resolved through the OS credential store.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="cp-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect x="20" y="30" width="200" height="90" rx="10" class="dg-box dg-strong" />
      <text x="120" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-title">1 · PNCLI_* env var</text>
      <text x="120" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-mono">PNCLI_GITHUB_TOKEN</text>
      <text x="120" y="104" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">always wins</text>

      <line x1="222" y1="75" x2="278" y2="75" class="dg-line" marker-end="url(#cp-arrow)" />
      <text x="250" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">not set</text>

      <rect x="280" y="30" width="200" height="90" rx="10" class="dg-box" />
      <text x="380" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-title">2 · CI fallback var</text>
      <text x="380" y="80" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-mono">GITHUB_TOKEN</text>
      <text x="380" y="96" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-mono">SONAR_TOKEN</text>
      <text x="380" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-mono">SYSTEM_ACCESSTOKEN</text>

      <line x1="482" y1="75" x2="538" y2="75" class="dg-line" marker-end="url(#cp-arrow)" />
      <text x="510" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">not set</text>

      <rect x="540" y="30" width="200" height="90" rx="10" class="dg-box dg-accent" />
      <text x="640" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-title">3 · global config</text>
      <text x="640" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-mono">~/.pncli/config.json</text>
      <text x="640" y="104" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">plaintext, or keychain: ref</text>

      <line x1="640" y1="122" x2="640" y2="158" class="dg-line dg-dashed" marker-end="url(#cp-arrow)" />
      <rect x="560" y="160" width="160" height="36" rx="8" class="dg-box dg-faint" />
      <text x="640" y="183" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">keychain: → OS store</text>

      <text x="20" y="160" class="dg-note">First match wins.</text>
      <text x="20" y="180" class="dg-sub">A repo's .pncli.json holds team defaults — never secrets.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink/50 font-mono">
    CI keeps working unchanged: env vars sit above anything stored on disk. Set <code>PNCLI_KEYCHAIN_BACKEND=none</code> to ignore keychain references on a runner.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
